    "sourcePath": "docs/help/guides/conversations-and-notifications.md",
    "content": "## Choose a Conversation\nUse a project channel for communication the project team should find with the job record, a direct message for private coordination, a staff channel for ongoing company discussion, and an announcement for important audience-wide information. Do not leave a project decision only in a private message when the project team needs its record.\n\n## Send a Message\nOpen the correct channel, confirm its name and project context, write the message, mention only people whose attention is required, attach permitted files, and send. Include searchable context such as the project number, subject, company, or scope.\n\nMentions may trigger in-app, email, push, or text notifications according to the recipient's preferences and configured services.\n\n## Attachments\nUse the composer attachment control and open the result after sending. A project-channel file should live in the mapped project Drive location, and intended recipients must have permission to open it. A preview in a conversation does not change the file's project-wide visibility.\n\n## Message Actions\nEdit your own message to correct a mistake when allowed. Delete only when the removal is permitted and appropriate for the project record. Reactions are quick acknowledgments, not formal approvals. Archive an inactive channel when its history should remain searchable.\n\n## Announcements\nAuthorized staff can create an announcement and select its audience. Choose narrowly: staff, owners, project partners, or everyone only when the content truly applies. An organization-wide announcement is not a substitute for a project message.\n\n## Notification Preferences\nIn **Settings**, confirm the timezone and choose supported in-app, email, push, and text notifications. SMS requires the user's own current consent. Save changes and use a test action when available; never enable text delivery for another person without consent.\n\n## Quick Check\n- [ ] I intentionally chose project, direct, staff, or announcement context.\n- [ ] The message contains enough context to find later.\n- [ ] Attachments open for intended recipients.\n- [ ] Important decisions remain in a durable project record.",
