    "content": "## Start an Update\nThe preferred workflow starts in **Daily Logs**: filter to the reporting period, select only appropriate logs, and choose **Draft owner update**. You can also open **Owner Updates** from the project to review existing drafts and published updates.\n\n## Review the Draft\nCheck the title and period, project and owner information, summary, work completed, next steps, schedule language, selected photos, captions, and links. Remove duplicate or internal metadata and distinguish confirmed commitments from tentative plans.\n\n## Photo and Audience Safety\nUse only photos approved for owner visibility. Open them at full size and inspect receipts, personal information, issue documentation, and background details before including them. Owner visibility does not mean public visibility.\n\n## Publish and Share\nPublishing changes a working draft into an approved owner-facing record. Confirm required project-manager review first. Sharing controls may provide a print/save-PDF view, Compass link, or prepared email. Review the actual output and recipient access before sending.\n\nUse the deployed Compass address, not a local or preview URL. A Compass link cannot override a restricted Drive file's sharing settings.\n\n## Correct a Published Update\nDo not quietly overwrite a material client communication. Notify the project manager or administrator and preserve a clear correction trail.\n\n## Quick Check\n- [ ] The reporting period and included logs match.\n- [ ] Text is concise, client-facing, and final.\n- [ ] Every photo is approved for the owner.\n- [ ] Links and recipient access were tested.\n- [ ] The final view was reviewed before sharing.",
