    "content": "## Upload and Find Photos\nOpen project **Photos**, choose files, confirm the date, type, caption, and phase, then upload. Originals belong in the mapped Drive location while Compass stores project relationships and display metadata. New uploads begin internal and awaiting review.\n\nUse date, phase, type, review, visibility, and sort controls to narrow the library. Filters never change permission by themselves.\n\n## Review the Full Image\nOpen the full image before approving it. Confirm the project, date, phase, type, orientation, clarity, and background details. A suggested phase is not approval.\n\nLook for faces, addresses, license plates, receipts, safety incidents, disputes, defects, internal notes, or other information that should remain limited.\n\n## Approve and Set Visibility\nSelect the intended photos and apply a type and each permitted audience. If no external audience is selected, the photo remains internal. Use **Reject** when it should not enter the approved project library.\n\n- **Owner** exposes it to assigned owners according to project access.\n- **Subs/vendors** exposes it to assigned project partners as permitted.\n- **Public** approves it for a broader sharing workflow.\n\nThese choices are independent. Owner-visible is not public, and public approval does not make the underlying Drive folder public.\n\n## Logs and Owner Updates\nAttaching a photo to a daily log does not make it owner-visible. An owner update should include a photo only after approval and owner visibility are confirmed.\n\n## Batch Actions\nUse filtered selection only after reviewing the active filters. Confirm every selected image before applying visibility. Compass clears selection after an action so an earlier batch is not accidentally reused.\n\n## Quick Check\n- [ ] I opened the full-size image.\n- [ ] Project, date, phase, and type are correct.\n- [ ] Owner, partner, and public visibility were considered separately.\n- [ ] Sensitive issue or delivery documentation remains internal unless authorized.",
